####  func [¶](https://pkg.go.dev/context#Cause "Go to Cause") added in go1.20
```
func Cause(c Context[](https://pkg.go.dev/context#Context)) error[](https://pkg.go.dev/builtin#error)
```

Cause returns a non-nil error explaining why c was canceled. The first cancellation of c or one of its parents sets the cause. If that cancellation happened via a call to CancelCauseFunc(err), then [Cause](https://pkg.go.dev/context#Cause) returns err. Otherwise Cause(c) returns the same value as c.Err(). Cause returns nil if c has not been canceled yet. 
####  func [¶](https://pkg.go.dev/context#WithCancel "Go to WithCancel")
```
func WithCancel(parent Context[](https://pkg.go.dev/context#Context)) (ctx Context[](https://pkg.go.dev/context#Context), cancel CancelFunc[](https://pkg.go.dev/context#CancelFunc))
```

WithCancel returns a copy of parent with a new Done channel. The returned context's Done channel is closed when the returned cancel function is called or when the parent context's Done channel is closed, whichever happens first. 
Canceling this context releases resources associated with it, so code should call cancel as soon as the operations running in this [Context](https://pkg.go.dev/context#Context) complete. 
